Open recalls are worse for pickups than

286
00:10:16,290 --> 00:10:17,182
you might think.

287
00:10:17,362 --> 00:10:20,461
In Canada, Carfax Canada reported that crew

288
00:10:20,461 --> 00:10:23,056
cab pickups were among the top three

289
00:10:23,056 --> 00:10:26,011
vehicle types for reported recalls in its

290
00:10:26,011 --> 00:10:27,741
twenty twenty-five data.

291
00:10:27,921 --> 00:10:31,358
And the biggest recalls of twenty twenty-five

292
00:10:31,358 --> 00:10:34,489
and twenty twenty-six were truck recalls,

293
00:10:34,489 --> 00:10:37,620
four point four million Fords for trailer

294
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:40,216
brakes, one and a half million Ram

295
00:10:40,216 --> 00:10:43,576
fifteen hundreds for rear seat belt anchors,

296
00:10:43,576 --> 00:10:46,555
and one point four million older F-150s

297
00:10:46,555 --> 00:10:48,540
for unexpected downshifts.

298
00:10:48,890 --> 00:10:51,149
The good news is that this warning

299
00:10:51,149 --> 00:10:52,942
sign is the easiest to fix.

300
00:10:53,122 --> 00:10:55,142
Recall repairs are free.

301
00:10:55,322 --> 00:10:57,379
So an open recall is not a

302
00:10:57,379 --> 00:10:59,990
reason to walk away from a truck.

303
00:11:00,170 --> 00:11:01,946
It is a reason to know before

304
00:11:01,946 --> 00:11:03,722
you buy, and to get it fixed.

305
00:11:03,902 --> 00:11:05,998
Carfax Canada's president,

306
00:11:05,998 --> 00:11:08,175
Shawn Vording, put it well.

307
00:11:08,355 --> 00:11:10,798
A recall or an accident does not

308
00:11:10,798 --> 00:11:13,776
automatically make a used vehicle a bad

309
00:11:13,776 --> 00:11:14,311
choice.

310
00:11:14,491 --> 00:11:16,793
What matters is that buyers know about

311
00:11:16,793 --> 00:11:16,975
it.

312
00:11:17,325 --> 00:11:18,742
So how do you check?

313
00:11:18,922 --> 00:11:21,694
Go to the federal safety website,

314
00:11:21,694 --> 00:11:24,046
NHTSA dot gov slash recalls,

315
00:11:24,046 --> 00:11:26,903
enter the seventeen-character VIN,

316
00:11:26,903 --> 00:11:27,827
and search.

317
00:11:28,007 --> 00:11:28,924
It takes a minute.

318
00:11:29,104 --> 00:11:32,527
Then check the manufacturer's own recall page

319
00:11:32,527 --> 00:11:32,831
too.

320
00:11:33,011 --> 00:11:34,993
If there is a recall with a

321
00:11:34,993 --> 00:11:36,534
do not drive warning,

322
00:11:36,534 --> 00:11:39,984
like the twenty twenty-six Maverick control arm

323
00:11:39,984 --> 00:11:41,306
recall we covered,

324
00:11:41,306 --> 00:11:43,728
do not drive the truck home until

325
00:11:43,728 --> 00:11:44,609
it is fixed.

326
00:11:44,789 --> 00:11:46,978
And if a seller says the recall

327
00:11:46,978 --> 00:11:49,096
was done, ask for the invoice.

328
00:11:49,446 --> 00:11:51,398
And the tools to check are better

329
00:11:51,398 --> 00:11:51,989
than ever.

330
00:11:52,169 --> 00:11:54,201
In March twenty twenty-six,

331
00:11:54,201 --> 00:11:57,362
Carfax said its free recall search service

332
00:11:57,362 --> 00:11:58,415
had checked U.

333
00:11:58,595 --> 00:11:59,048
S.

334
00:11:59,228 --> 00:12:01,760
vehicles more than ten billion times,

335
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:04,223
and that more than thirty million of

336
00:12:04,223 --> 00:12:06,960
the open recalls it found were repaired.

337
00:12:07,140 --> 00:12:11,074
Eight state motor vehicle departments use it,

338
00:12:11,074 --> 00:12:13,784
including California, New York,

339
00:12:13,784 --> 00:12:15,883
Ohio, Arizona and Texas.

340
00:12:16,063 --> 00:12:17,722
When owners are told,

341
00:12:17,722 --> 00:12:19,302
many do get the fix.

342
00:12:19,482 --> 00:12:22,152
The problem is the trucks nobody checks.

343
00:12:22,501 --> 00:12:25,305
Warning sign number four is a hard-use

344
00:12:25,305 --> 00:12:27,076
history with no records.

345
00:12:27,256 --> 00:12:28,510
Trucks are tools.

346
00:12:28,690 --> 00:12:31,546
Many used trucks have spent years towing,

347
00:12:31,546 --> 00:12:33,636
plowing, carrying heavy loads,

348
00:12:33,636 --> 00:12:35,168
or working in a fleet.

349
00:12:35,348 --> 00:12:37,113
That is not automatically bad.

350
00:12:37,293 --> 00:12:39,638
Heavy-duty trucks are built for it.

351
00:12:39,818 --> 00:12:42,320
But hard use changes which problems you

352
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:43,346
should look for,

353
00:12:43,346 --> 00:12:45,656
and without records you have no idea

354
00:12:45,656 --> 00:12:47,388
what has already been done.

355
00:12:47,738 --> 00:12:49,658
Look at how many of the recalls

356
00:12:49,658 --> 00:12:51,951
and problems we have covered are tied

357
00:12:51,951 --> 00:12:53,438
to towing and heavy use.

358
00:12:53,618 --> 00:12:56,934
Ford's recall of about one hundred three

359
00:12:56,934 --> 00:13:00,168
thousand F-150s for rear axle hub bolts

360
00:13:00,168 --> 00:13:03,070
that can snap was limited to trucks

361
00:13:03,070 --> 00:13:05,806
with the heaviest-duty rear axle,

362
00:13:05,806 --> 00:13:07,713
according to RV Travel.

363
00:13:07,893 --> 00:13:11,072
The Super Duty's low-pressure fuel pump problem

364
00:13:11,072 --> 00:13:13,304
was more likely with low fuel and

365
00:13:13,304 --> 00:13:14,115
hot weather.

366
00:13:14,295 --> 00:13:17,390
And trailer module recalls only matter if

367
00:13:17,390 --> 00:13:18,521
the truck tows.

368
00:13:18,701 --> 00:13:20,829
The work a truck has done shapes

369
00:13:20,829 --> 00:13:21,627
what breaks.

370
00:13:21,978 --> 00:13:23,406
Here is the twist.

371
00:13:23,586 --> 00:13:26,186
Records matter even more than mileage.

372
00:13:26,366 --> 00:13:29,402
In the federal investigation of GM's six

373
00:13:29,402 --> 00:13:30,389
point two V8,

374
00:13:30,389 --> 00:13:32,969
owners who can prove the right oil

375
00:13:32,969 --> 00:13:35,550
was used are in the best position.

376
00:13:35,730 --> 00:13:38,485
In the Ford diesel fuel pump lawsuit,

377
00:13:38,485 --> 00:13:41,612
Ford argued some failures came from owners

378
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:43,995
who did not change fuel filters,

379
00:13:43,995 --> 00:13:46,898
according to Pickup Truck and SUV Talk.

380
00:13:47,078 --> 00:13:49,140
A truck with high miles and a

381
00:13:49,140 --> 00:13:51,486
thick folder of receipts can be a

382
00:13:51,486 --> 00:13:54,045
safer buy than a low-mile truck with

383
00:13:54,045 --> 00:13:54,613
nothing.

384
00:13:54,963 --> 00:13:56,949
So how do you spot hard use?

385
00:13:57,129 --> 00:13:59,474
Look at the hitch receiver for heavy

386
00:13:59,474 --> 00:14:02,014
wear, and check whether a trailer brake

387
00:14:02,014 --> 00:14:03,642
controller was installed.

388
00:14:03,822 --> 00:14:05,954
Look under the truck for bent or

389
00:14:05,954 --> 00:14:06,887
scraped parts.

390
00:14:07,067 --> 00:14:09,203
Check the bed for deep damage.

391
00:14:09,383 --> 00:14:11,818
Look for a lift kit or oversized

392
00:14:11,818 --> 00:14:15,318
tires, which change the front-end geometry and

393
00:14:15,318 --> 00:14:18,285
can make problems like the death wobble

394
00:14:18,285 --> 00:14:20,796
more likely on solid-axle trucks.

395
00:14:20,976 --> 00:14:23,208
Then ask for the service history,

396
00:14:23,208 --> 00:14:24,628
and if there is none,

397
00:14:24,628 --> 00:14:26,792
price that risk into your offer.

398
00:14:27,142 --> 00:14:29,332
And to be fair to work trucks,

399
00:14:29,332 --> 00:14:31,302
hard use is not the same as

400
00:14:31,302 --> 00:14:31,740
abuse.

401
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:35,194
iSeeCars found that heavy-duty trucks last up

402
00:14:35,194 --> 00:14:38,105
to twice as long as light-duty versions,

403
00:14:38,105 --> 00:14:40,360
according to Work Truck Online.

404
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:42,790
A fleet truck that was serviced on

405
00:14:42,790 --> 00:14:44,907
schedule by a business can be in

406
00:14:44,907 --> 00:14:47,421
better shape than a weekend truck that

407
00:14:47,421 --> 00:14:48,215
was ignored.

408
00:14:48,395 --> 00:14:50,475
The warning sign is not that the

409
00:14:50,475 --> 00:14:51,320
truck worked.

410
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:53,385
It is that nobody can show you

411
00:14:53,385 --> 00:14:54,705
how it was cared for.

412
00:14:55,055 --> 00:14:57,711
Warning sign number five is a specific

413
00:14:57,711 --> 00:15:00,087
engine and model year with a known

414
00:15:00,087 --> 00:15:03,163
problem, combined with a cold-start test the

415
00:15:03,163 --> 00:15:05,329
seller does not want you to do.

416
00:15:05,509 --> 00:15:08,607
In earlier videos we covered the documented

417
00:15:08,607 --> 00:15:09,039
cases.

418
00:15:09,219 --> 00:15:12,541
Toyota's twin-turbo V6 in twenty twenty-two to

419
00:15:12,541 --> 00:15:14,491
twenty twenty-four Tundras,

420
00:15:14,491 --> 00:15:17,381
with three recalls for machining debris.

421
00:15:17,561 --> 00:15:20,268
GM's six point two in engines built

422
00:15:20,268 --> 00:15:23,518
from March twenty twenty-one to May twenty

423
00:15:23,518 --> 00:15:26,999
twenty-four, now under federal investigation.

424
00:15:27,350 --> 00:15:30,405
Ford's three point five EcoBoost cam phaser

425
00:15:30,405 --> 00:15:33,461
issues on twenty seventeen to twenty twenty

426
00:15:33,461 --> 00:15:36,162
trucks, with no recall and an extended

427
00:15:36,162 --> 00:15:39,217
warranty that ended in twenty twenty-three,

428
00:15:39,217 --> 00:15:40,852
according to SlashGear.

429
00:15:41,032 --> 00:15:45,273
GM's eight-speed transmission shudder on twenty fifteen

430
00:15:45,273 --> 00:15:47,277
to twenty nineteen trucks,

431
00:15:47,277 --> 00:15:50,053
and its ten-speed valve body recall.

432
00:15:50,233 --> 00:15:53,261
And the Ram EcoDiesel's EGR cooler recall

433
00:15:53,261 --> 00:15:56,584
on twenty fourteen to twenty nineteen trucks.

434
00:15:56,764 --> 00:15:58,990
None of these mean every truck is

435
00:15:58,990 --> 00:15:59,260
bad.

436
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:01,295
They mean you know exactly what to

437
00:16:01,295 --> 00:16:01,622
check.

438
00:16:01,973 --> 00:16:03,528
Here is the twist.

439
00:16:03,708 --> 00:16:06,064
Many of these problems show up most

440
00:16:06,064 --> 00:16:07,679
clearly on a cold start.

441
00:16:07,859 --> 00:16:10,303
The EcoBoost cam phaser rattle is a

442
00:16:10,303 --> 00:16:12,538
few seconds of noise at startup.

443
00:16:12,718 --> 00:16:14,705
A lifter tick on a GM V8

444
00:16:14,705 --> 00:16:16,526
is often loudest cold.

445
00:16:16,706 --> 00:16:20,003
A transmission that engages harshly cold may

446
00:16:20,003 --> 00:16:21,652
feel normal once warm.

447
00:16:21,832 --> 00:16:24,043
So if you arrive for a test

448
00:16:24,043 --> 00:16:27,074
drive and the engine is already warm,

449
00:16:27,074 --> 00:16:27,729
ask why.

450
00:16:27,909 --> 00:16:29,786
A seller who warmed up the truck

451
00:16:29,786 --> 00:16:31,781
before you got there may be hiding

452
00:16:31,781 --> 00:16:33,540
exactly what you came to hear.

453
00:16:33,891 --> 00:16:35,400
So how do you check?

454
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:37,445
Ask the seller not to start the

455
00:16:37,445 --> 00:16:38,889
truck before you arrive.

456
00:16:39,069 --> 00:16:40,715
Put your hand on the hood when

457
00:16:40,715 --> 00:16:41,484
you get there.

458
00:16:41,664 --> 00:16:43,993
Start it yourself and listen for the

459
00:16:43,993 --> 00:16:45,158
first ten seconds.

460
00:16:45,338 --> 00:16:46,296
Then drive it,

461
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:48,554
and feel every shift from park to

462
00:16:48,554 --> 00:16:51,155
drive and below twenty miles per hour.

463
00:16:51,335 --> 00:16:53,162
If the truck has one of the

464
00:16:53,162 --> 00:16:54,583
engines we mentioned,

465
00:16:54,583 --> 00:16:57,223
ask whether the recall or warranty work

466
00:16:57,223 --> 00:16:59,659
was done, and ask for the paperwork.

467
00:17:00,009 --> 00:17:02,806
And heavy-duty buyers have one more thing

468
00:17:02,806 --> 00:17:03,352
to test.

469
00:17:03,532 --> 00:17:06,675
According to Pickup Truck and SUV Talk's

470
00:17:06,675 --> 00:17:09,189
report on Consumer Reports data,

471
00:17:09,189 --> 00:17:13,353
some Ram heavy-duty owners reported software problems

472
00:17:13,353 --> 00:17:16,575
that left trucks limited to about fifteen

473
00:17:16,575 --> 00:17:17,753
miles per hour,

474
00:17:17,753 --> 00:17:20,425
or made tow haul mode unavailable.

475
00:17:20,605 --> 00:17:22,899
So on any heavy-duty test drive,

476
00:17:22,899 --> 00:17:25,337
switch into tow haul mode and make

477
00:17:25,337 --> 00:17:26,341
sure it works,

478
00:17:26,341 --> 00:17:28,778
and check the dash for any warning

479
00:17:28,778 --> 00:17:31,216
messages before you leave the lot.

480
00:17:31,567 --> 00:17:34,111
And here is a bonus warning sign,

481
00:17:34,111 --> 00:17:35,421
accident history.

482
00:17:35,601 --> 00:17:37,935
In its twenty twenty-five data,

483
00:17:37,935 --> 00:17:40,870
Carfax Canada said one in four vehicles

484
00:17:40,870 --> 00:17:43,656
searched on its reports had damage or

485
00:17:43,656 --> 00:17:44,935
accident history.

486
00:17:45,115 --> 00:17:47,441
An accident does not make a truck

487
00:17:47,441 --> 00:17:48,146
a bad buy.

488
00:17:48,326 --> 00:17:49,584
But a hidden one,

489
00:17:49,584 --> 00:17:51,213
or one repaired badly,

490
00:17:51,213 --> 00:17:52,546
can affect safety,

491
00:17:52,546 --> 00:17:55,285
especially on a truck whose frame and

492
00:17:55,285 --> 00:17:57,358
structure carry heavy loads.

493
00:17:57,538 --> 00:18:00,195
Look for paint that does not match,

494
00:18:00,195 --> 00:18:02,245
uneven gaps between panels,

495
00:18:02,245 --> 00:18:04,446
and overspray on rubber trim.

496
00:18:04,797 --> 00:18:07,454
And remember the safety ratings we covered

497
00:18:07,454 --> 00:18:08,593
in the last video.

498
00:18:08,773 --> 00:18:11,846
A used truck's crash protection depends on

499
00:18:11,846 --> 00:18:15,359
its structure being repaired correctly after any

500
00:18:15,359 --> 00:18:16,018
accident.

501
00:18:16,198 --> 00:18:19,468
If a history report shows structural damage

502
00:18:19,468 --> 00:18:21,066
or airbag deployment,

503
00:18:21,066 --> 00:18:22,967
that is a reason to get a

504
00:18:22,967 --> 00:18:26,542
professional inspection, not just a test drive.

505
00:18:26,722 --> 00:18:29,031
The cost of an inspection is tiny

506
00:18:29,031 --> 00:18:31,620
compared with the cost of finding out

507
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:32,040
later.

508
00:18:32,390 --> 00:18:34,770
So look at all five warning signs

509
00:18:34,770 --> 00:18:35,420
together.

510
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:37,504
Mileage that does not add up.

511
00:18:37,684 --> 00:18:39,019
Signs of water.

512
00:18:39,199 --> 00:18:40,615
An open recall.

513
00:18:40,795 --> 00:18:42,699
Hard use with no records.

514
00:18:42,879 --> 00:18:45,669
And a problem engine or transmission that

515
00:18:45,669 --> 00:18:47,233
sounds wrong when cold.

516
00:18:47,413 --> 00:18:49,390
Notice that three of them can be

517
00:18:49,390 --> 00:18:50,872
checked online for free,

518
00:18:50,872 --> 00:18:52,046
using only the VIN.

519
00:18:52,226 --> 00:18:54,013
The other two need your eyes,

520
00:18:54,013 --> 00:18:55,616
your ears, and a mechanic.

521
00:18:55,796 --> 00:18:57,612
Every one of them can be checked

522
00:18:57,612 --> 00:18:59,372
before you hand over any money.

523
00:18:59,722 --> 00:19:01,533
And here is the final twist.

524
00:19:01,713 --> 00:19:04,575
None of these warning signs automatically means

525
00:19:04,575 --> 00:19:05,184
walk away.

526
00:19:05,364 --> 00:19:07,531
A truck with an open recall can

527
00:19:07,531 --> 00:19:08,789
be fixed for free.

528
00:19:08,969 --> 00:19:11,281
A truck with high miles and great

529
00:19:11,281 --> 00:19:13,172
records can be a great buy.

530
00:19:13,352 --> 00:19:15,424
Even a truck with an accident in

531
00:19:15,424 --> 00:19:17,302
its history can be fine if it

532
00:19:17,302 --> 00:19:18,727
was repaired properly.

533
00:19:18,907 --> 00:19:20,951
The danger is not the problem.

534
00:19:21,131 --> 00:19:23,336
The danger is not knowing about it,

535
00:19:23,336 --> 00:19:25,037
and paying as if it was not

536
00:19:25,037 --> 00:19:25,415
there.

537
00:19:25,765 --> 00:19:28,112
So here is your used truck checklist

538
00:19:28,112 --> 00:19:29,677
for twenty twenty-seven.

539
00:19:29,857 --> 00:19:32,391
One, run the VIN on the federal

540
00:19:32,391 --> 00:19:35,415
recall site and get a vehicle history

541
00:19:35,415 --> 00:19:35,987
report.

542
00:19:36,167 --> 00:19:39,171
Two, run the free flood and odometer

543
00:19:39,171 --> 00:19:39,755
checks.

544
00:19:39,935 --> 00:19:42,977
Three, compare the mileage with every record.

545
00:19:43,157 --> 00:19:44,921
Four, do the smell,

546
00:19:44,921 --> 00:19:47,522
carpet, rust and silt check.

547
00:19:47,702 --> 00:19:51,196
Five, start the engine cold yourself.

548
00:19:51,376 --> 00:19:53,376
Six, look at the hitch,

549
00:19:53,376 --> 00:19:54,941
bed and underbody.

550
00:19:55,121 --> 00:19:58,305
And seven, pay for an independent inspection

551
00:19:58,305 --> 00:19:59,463
before you sign.

552
00:19:59,813 --> 00:20:01,324
We put this checklist,

553
00:20:01,324 --> 00:20:03,796
plus the engines and years to watch,

554
00:20:03,796 --> 00:20:07,162
into the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide.

555
00:20:07,342 --> 00:20:09,477
The link is in the description and

556
00:20:09,477 --> 00:20:10,860
in the pinned comment.

557
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:12,113
If this helped,

558
00:20:12,113 --> 00:20:14,833
subscribe, because next we look at the

559
00:20:14,833 --> 00:20:16,980
most stolen trucks in America,

560
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:18,841
and why thieves love them.

561
00:20:19,021 --> 00:20:20,672
And tell us in the comments,

562
00:20:20,672 --> 00:20:22,853
which warning sign have you run into?

563
00:20:23,033 --> 00:20:24,078
Thanks for watching.
